---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { company } from '../data/company';
---

<Base
  title="About"
  description="KCNEX Innovations is a small product company building software that protects people from online scams. Built in India, serving families in the US, UK, and Canada."
>
  <section class="section">
    <div class="container">
      <p class="eyebrow">About</p>
      <h1 class="page-title">A small company with a narrow focus</h1>

      <div class="prose lede">
        <p>
          KCNEX Innovations builds consumer software that protects people
          online. We are small, we are self-directed, and we work on one class
          of problem at a time.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="prose body">
        <h2>Why we exist</h2>
        <p>
          Our first product started with a specific incident: a founder watched
          a family member nearly lose everything to a tech-support scam. A fake
          pop-up, a phone number, and a request to install remote-access
          software. It was textbook — and it very nearly worked.
        </p>
        <p>
          The uncomfortable part was that every piece of technology needed to
          stop it already existed. It had simply never been assembled for the
          person actually at risk. That gap is what KCNEX exists to close.
        </p>

        <h2>What we are, honestly</h2>
        <p>
          We are a small team, not an enterprise. We are built in {company.builtIn},
          and our products serve families in the {company.serves.join(', ')}. We
          would rather tell you that plainly than dress it up — you can judge
          the software on what it does.
        </p>
        <p>
          KCNEX is the company. <a href="https://kinsentry.com">KinSentry</a> is
          what we have shipped so far. As we build more, each product will stand
          on its own and each will be listed on this site.
        </p>

        <h2>How we think about trust</h2>
        <p>
          Protective software asks for a lot of trust: it sits between someone
          and their browser, at exactly the moment they are most vulnerable. We
          think that trust is earned by being boring and verifiable — publishing
          what we collect, answering security reports, and never claiming more
          than we can demonstrate.
        </p>
        <p>
          If you find something on this site that is inaccurate, we want to know.
          Write to <a href={`mailto:${company.email.general}`}>{company.email.general}</a>.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>

<style>
  .page-title {
    font-size: clamp(36px, 6vw, 60px);
    max-width: 18ch;
    margin-bottom: 24px;
  }

  .lede {
    font-size: clamp(17px, 2vw, 20px);
    padding-bottom: 8px;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border);
  }

  .body {
    margin-top: 8px;
  }
</style>
